1
00:00:01,168 --> 00:00:02,295
<i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:02,436 --> 00:00:03,546
GORDON: <i>Word
of the chemical spill</i>

3
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,730
- reached the mainland.
- Reunification
isn't happening.

4
00:00:06,039 --> 00:00:07,302
No action until the government

5
00:00:07,441 --> 00:00:09,000
can determine if Gotham's safe.

6
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:12,601
OSWALD: I sentence
you, Victor Zsasz, to die.

7
00:00:12,746 --> 00:00:14,339
- (gunshot)
- (gasping, screaming)

8
00:00:14,481 --> 00:00:15,481
Get him out of there!

9
00:00:16,783 --> 00:00:18,649
What the hell are you doing?!

10
00:00:18,785 --> 00:00:21,152
Trying to keep you all from
making a terrible mistake.

11
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:23,254
- Her name is Ivy.
- She's a witch.

12
00:00:25,425 --> 00:00:28,589
I'm feeding the earth with
these wretched creatures.

13
00:00:28,729 --> 00:00:30,095
It consumes them,

14
00:00:30,364 --> 00:00:31,491
and then it flourishes.

15
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,042
We wouldn't have
escaped without you.

16
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:34,066
You saved me

17
00:00:34,101 --> 00:00:34,761
<i>and my friends.</i>

18
00:00:35,102 --> 00:00:36,102
I wanted to help.

19
00:00:41,074 --> 00:00:42,508
- Come with us.
- Are you telling me

20
00:00:42,643 --> 00:00:43,843
you found a way out of Gotham?

21
00:00:44,111 --> 00:00:45,170
It's a submarine.

22
00:00:45,312 --> 00:00:46,439
I've been giving you space,

23
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,258
but we have to talk about
how this is gonna work.

24
00:00:48,282 --> 00:00:49,425
I'm gonna be a
part of this kid's life.

25
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:51,714
- Oh, you seem pretty confident
about that.
- I am.

26
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,714
You're having a
baby with Barbara.

27
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:55,782
Can't change the past, so...

28
00:00:56,123 --> 00:00:57,563
I guess we just
have to live with it.

29
00:01:04,264 --> 00:01:05,698
(indistinct chatter)

30
00:01:05,832 --> 00:01:06,663
Come on, people!

31
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,393
Time's a-wastin'!

32
00:01:10,237 --> 00:01:12,797
The filtration system that
Lucius designed is working.

33
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:15,700
What you're doing is both
unnecessary and it's reckless.

34
00:01:15,842 --> 00:01:18,676
Our supplies of drinking
water are at critical levels.

35
00:01:18,845 --> 00:01:20,609
Every day, the gangs
grow more aggressive.

36
00:01:20,747 --> 00:01:23,148
If I can get a cease-fire,
even a temporary one,

37
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:25,276
then when reunification
does happen,

38
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:27,149
at least there will be
people left to save.

39
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:28,482
They deserve that much.

40
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:30,318
And does your child
deserve a father?

41
00:01:30,457 --> 00:01:32,457
You have no problem
taking care of the entire city.

42
00:01:32,492 --> 00:01:34,358
What about focusing
on just one life?

43
00:01:34,494 --> 00:01:35,805
<i>(sighs) Why are
you always so ready</i>

44
00:01:35,829 --> 00:01:37,354
<i>to put yourself
in the crosshairs?</i>

45
00:01:37,531 --> 00:01:40,501
It's like you won't be satisfied
until you sacrifice yourself.

46
00:01:41,368 --> 00:01:42,233
You really believe that?

47
00:01:42,369 --> 00:01:43,098
<i>I do.</i>

48
00:01:43,337 --> 00:01:44,737
And it scares me.

49
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,740
How is this gonna work?

50
00:01:48,375 --> 00:01:49,695
Am I supposed to
just stay at home

51
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:51,369
and raise this
child with Barbara

52
00:01:51,511 --> 00:01:53,742
while you go cowboying
off all the time?

53
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,473
It won't always be like this.

54
00:01:55,816 --> 00:01:56,816
After reunification...

55
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:58,311
Nothing will be different.

56
00:01:58,518 --> 00:01:59,713
Unless you stop being...

57
00:01:59,853 --> 00:02:00,853
Me?

58
00:02:02,222 --> 00:02:03,222
BULLOCK: <i>Hey, Jim.</i>

59
00:02:04,257 --> 00:02:05,316
(exhales) I have to go.

60
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:07,655
- We'll talk after.
- If there is an after.

61
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:18,371
- (shouting)
- (chainsaw buzzing)

62
00:02:26,913 --> 00:02:28,711
Oh, yeah?! Oh-ho!

63
00:02:30,517 --> 00:02:32,486
Oswald, where the hell is Nygma?

64
00:02:32,619 --> 00:02:34,349
Shouldn't we have
left the city already?

65
00:02:35,322 --> 00:02:36,322
Ms. Kean,

66
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:38,454
this may come as a surprise,

67
00:02:38,592 --> 00:02:40,720
but building a
submarine from scratch

68
00:02:40,861 --> 00:02:42,796
by yourself takes time.

69
00:02:42,896 --> 00:02:44,626
- Patience.
- Easy for you to say.

70
00:02:44,765 --> 00:02:46,495
You're not a walking egg timer.

71
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,368
Tell him to get a move on.

72
00:02:48,568 --> 00:02:49,831
And why, exactly,

73
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:52,010
are you hosting Gordon's
gangland get-together?

74
00:02:52,806 --> 00:02:55,776
Keep your friends close and
your enemies closer, my dear.

75
00:02:56,343 --> 00:02:57,787
If we're really going
to leave Gotham,

76
00:02:57,811 --> 00:02:59,279
we need to keep Gordon happy.

77
00:03:00,447 --> 00:03:02,313
You know all about
that, don't you?

78
00:03:02,716 --> 00:03:04,344
It was a momentary slip.

79
00:03:04,718 --> 00:03:06,277
The world was on fire.

80
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,420
(loud thump)

81
00:03:07,587 --> 00:03:09,488
(indistinct shouting)

82
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:14,457
OSWALD: <i>Jim,</i>

83
00:03:14,594 --> 00:03:15,653
it's your show.

84
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:17,789
<i>Mi casa, su casa.</i>

85
00:03:21,401 --> 00:03:22,926
I'll make this short.

86
00:03:23,904 --> 00:03:25,395
Gotham is running dry.

87
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:27,934
Our supply of clean water

88
00:03:28,275 --> 00:03:30,244
will only last a
few more months.

89
00:03:31,545 --> 00:03:32,911
So you have a choice.

90
00:03:34,414 --> 00:03:35,780
You can keep killing each other,

91
00:03:35,916 --> 00:03:38,351
<i>fighting over what
little water is left,</i>

92
00:03:38,485 --> 00:03:40,545
<i>maybe eke out a few
more months, then die.</i>

93
00:03:41,254 --> 00:03:42,254
Or...

94
00:03:42,989 --> 00:03:45,254
we can all agree right now

95
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:46,655
to an immediate cease-fire.

96
00:03:46,793 --> 00:03:49,820
(scoffing, chattering)

97
00:03:49,963 --> 00:03:51,329
(speaks indistinctly)

98
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,733
The government will
not annex a war zone.

99
00:03:56,369 --> 00:03:59,635
If we can show them that we
deserve to rejoin the mainland,

100
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,468
supply chain will be restored

101
00:04:01,608 --> 00:04:04,578
and we will all survive
until reunification.

102
00:04:06,546 --> 00:04:07,741
<i>That's the choice.</i>

103
00:04:08,815 --> 00:04:09,815
Life or death.

104
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:11,381
Your call.

105
00:04:11,518 --> 00:04:14,454
(indistinct chatter)

106
00:04:22,462 --> 00:04:23,930
(chatter stops)

107
00:04:24,664 --> 00:04:25,893
- (gunshot)
- (gasping)

108
00:04:26,032 --> 00:04:27,364
Weapons down!

109
00:04:27,501 --> 00:04:28,696
Get back!

110
00:04:29,402 --> 00:04:30,961
Jim, you see where
the shooter was?

111
00:04:31,638 --> 00:04:32,638
Jim.

112
00:04:37,477 --> 00:04:38,477
Oh, my God.

113
00:04:39,679 --> 00:04:41,614
♪♪

114
00:04:43,984 --> 00:04:45,919
♪♪

115
00:04:50,524 --> 00:04:52,356
- (indistinct chatter)
- (labored breathing)

116
00:04:52,726 --> 00:04:53,726
BULLOCK: <i>Get back!</i>

117
00:04:54,694 --> 00:04:55,855
You're gonna be all right.

118
00:04:55,996 --> 00:04:57,760
It's bad. We got
to move him. Now.

119
00:04:57,898 --> 00:04:59,764
Clinic's too far. M.E.'s office.

120
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:00,900
Alvarez, come on. Help.

121
00:05:01,001 --> 00:05:02,001
On it.

122
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:04,298
Take my gun.

123
00:05:04,437 --> 00:05:06,338
- (groaning)
- One, two, three.

124
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:07,702
All right. Get back.

125
00:05:07,841 --> 00:05:10,367
- Back! Get back!
- (shouting)

126
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:15,445
Well,

127
00:05:15,582 --> 00:05:16,743
I did not see that coming.

128
00:05:20,387 --> 00:05:22,322
- (siren wailing in distance)
- (bell clanging)

129
00:05:25,959 --> 00:05:27,621
What made you choose this,

130
00:05:27,794 --> 00:05:29,057
of all places,

131
00:05:29,396 --> 00:05:30,864
for a scavenging mission?

132
00:05:32,532 --> 00:05:33,864
Just trust me, okay?

133
00:05:39,806 --> 00:05:41,570
What the hell?

134
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:49,040
("Cherry Blossom Moon" by
Rob Parton Orchestra playing)

135
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:56,689
Sit.

136
00:05:58,491 --> 00:05:59,515
(chuckles)

137
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:08,667
(chuckles softly)

138
00:06:14,941 --> 00:06:16,034
<i>Wow.</i>

139
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:17,634
<i>Candles.</i>

140
00:06:18,945 --> 00:06:20,065
If I didn't know any better,

141
00:06:20,113 --> 00:06:22,139
I'd say this was a... date.

142
00:06:28,755 --> 00:06:29,882
Maybe it is.

143
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:36,924
That okay with you?

144
00:06:38,632 --> 00:06:39,691
Maybe.

145
00:06:48,041 --> 00:06:49,134
Good.

146
00:06:52,012 --> 00:06:53,071
So let's eat.

147
00:07:01,187 --> 00:07:02,187
Lee!

148
00:07:02,689 --> 00:07:03,689
<i>It's Jim. He's lost</i>

149
00:07:03,823 --> 00:07:05,103
a lot of blood.
Can you save him?

150
00:07:07,727 --> 00:07:08,524
(exhales)

151
00:07:08,662 --> 00:07:09,662
Come with me!

152
00:07:10,864 --> 00:07:12,765
(indistinct chatter)

153
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:19,062
Doc says he's gonna be okay.

154
00:07:19,906 --> 00:07:21,499
He's gonna pull through.

155
00:07:22,475 --> 00:07:24,774
But until then,
I'm acting captain.

156
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:28,176
Now, the gangs of this city

157
00:07:28,815 --> 00:07:31,808
think this is their time
that they can run wild!

158
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:33,881
They are dead wrong!

159
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,679
I want us to take
to the streets.

160
00:07:35,889 --> 00:07:38,017
It is show-of-force time!

161
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:39,888
We ain't gonna give 'em an inch!

162
00:07:41,027 --> 00:07:42,027
Harper,

163
00:07:42,095 --> 00:07:43,723
I want you to
organize patrol teams.

164
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:45,030
What are you gonna do?

165
00:07:45,765 --> 00:07:47,927
I'm gonna find out
who shot my partner.

166
00:07:49,502 --> 00:07:51,494
THOMPKINS: The bullet
shattered against a rib.

167
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,175
I have to get all
the fragments out.

168
00:07:57,677 --> 00:07:58,474
(exhales)

169
00:07:58,611 --> 00:08:00,978
I haven't done general
surgery since med school.

170
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:04,950
There.

171
00:08:06,886 --> 00:08:07,930
All right, there's
an exit wound,

172
00:08:07,954 --> 00:08:09,547
so the rest must've
gone through.

173
00:08:09,689 --> 00:08:10,689
I need to sew him up.

174
00:08:10,890 --> 00:08:11,890
Can you get my kit?

175
00:08:11,925 --> 00:08:12,949
<i>Right away.</i>

176
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:18,123
Come on, Jim.

177
00:08:19,532 --> 00:08:21,572
(distantly): You can do
this, but you have to fight.

178
00:08:21,868 --> 00:08:22,961
You hear me?

179
00:08:24,771 --> 00:08:25,966
You have to fight.

180
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:28,607
♪♪

181
00:08:34,581 --> 00:08:36,516
(gavel banging)

182
00:08:38,785 --> 00:08:40,583
JUDGE: <i>Order in the court.</i>

183
00:08:41,621 --> 00:08:42,850
<i>James Gordon,</i>

184
00:08:43,156 --> 00:08:44,681
<i>you have been brought here</i>

185
00:08:44,824 --> 00:08:47,225
to be judged for
your many crimes,

186
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:50,155
and your very life
hangs in the balance.

187
00:08:50,964 --> 00:08:52,091
Do you understand?

188
00:08:52,665 --> 00:08:53,665
No, I...

189
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:55,961
The defendant understands

190
00:08:56,102 --> 00:08:57,195
and waives his right

191
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:58,732
<i>to appeal.</i>

192
00:08:59,305 --> 00:09:01,740
The trial of James Gordon

193
00:09:02,075 --> 00:09:04,840
will now begin.

194
00:09:05,845 --> 00:09:06,845
No! Wait!

195
00:09:11,885 --> 00:09:14,753
- (siren wailing in distance)
- (dog barking)

196
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:18,724
That...

197
00:09:19,292 --> 00:09:21,921
was the best canned
meal I've ever had.

198
00:09:22,962 --> 00:09:23,986
<i>And if this was a date,</i>

199
00:09:24,130 --> 00:09:25,207
<i>I don't know how
you're gonna top it</i>

200
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,927
when everything
gets back to normal.

201
00:09:31,037 --> 00:09:33,233
I don't think things are
ever gonna be normal.

202
00:09:33,807 --> 00:09:35,207
<i>For me, anyways.</i>

203
00:09:36,176 --> 00:09:37,667
What do you mean?

204
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:40,043
Wayne Manor's gone.

205
00:09:42,615 --> 00:09:44,495
And I know that a lot
of people lost a lot more,

206
00:09:44,651 --> 00:09:46,251
but part of me
wonders if it wasn't fate.

207
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:47,948
(sighs) It wasn't.

208
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:50,080
It was Jeremiah
blowing up your house.

209
00:09:51,157 --> 00:09:53,126
Maybe it's time to move on.

210
00:09:55,295 --> 00:09:57,855
You mean, like, leave Gotham?

211
00:09:58,665 --> 00:10:00,065
<i>Bruce, forget Wayne Manor.</i>

212
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:01,964
This city is your home.

213
00:10:03,203 --> 00:10:05,083
And how many terrible
things have happened to it

214
00:10:05,171 --> 00:10:06,332
because of me?

215
00:10:08,875 --> 00:10:10,036
Galavan.

216
00:10:11,311 --> 00:10:12,677
Ra's al Ghul.

217
00:10:18,017 --> 00:10:20,043
If this city really is my home,

218
00:10:21,721 --> 00:10:22,721
then maybe the best thing

219
00:10:22,856 --> 00:10:24,381
I can do for it is leave.

220
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:26,786
I have to say...

221
00:10:28,895 --> 00:10:30,864
kind of agree with
you on that one,

222
00:10:31,731 --> 00:10:33,199
billionaire boy.

223
00:10:34,033 --> 00:10:36,628
OSWALD: <i>Jim Gordon's
blood on my floor.</i>

224
00:10:36,903 --> 00:10:38,303
(groans) Olga!

225
00:10:38,805 --> 00:10:41,741
Why is the help never
around when you need them?

226
00:10:41,875 --> 00:10:42,934
(chuckling)

227
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:45,150
This could be good for us.

228
00:10:45,278 --> 00:10:46,278
You especially.

229
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,143
Are you serious?

230
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:52,380
Your baby daddy is
the top cop in Gotham.

231
00:10:53,052 --> 00:10:55,044
A dead Jim Gordon
is the only way

232
00:10:55,188 --> 00:10:57,020
you can hold
on to your little...

233
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:58,190
bundle of joy.

234
00:10:59,726 --> 00:11:01,092
Harvey, how is our dear...

235
00:11:01,227 --> 00:11:03,321
(grunts, gasps)

236
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:05,996
Who the hell did it?!
If I find out it was you,

237
00:11:06,199 --> 00:11:07,394
I swear to God...

238
00:11:07,734 --> 00:11:10,101
It wasn't me! I merely
supplied the venue!

239
00:11:10,203 --> 00:11:12,001
At your boss's request!

240
00:11:12,071 --> 00:11:13,664
That doesn't mean squat!

241
00:11:13,773 --> 00:11:16,242
Fine. You want to
know who's to blame?

242
00:11:16,376 --> 00:11:17,867
James Gordon!

243
00:11:18,011 --> 00:11:20,276
He invited every
criminal in Gotham!

244
00:11:20,413 --> 00:11:22,177
What did he think
was gonna happen?

245
00:11:22,282 --> 00:11:24,342
(grunts, coughs)

246
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:27,013
How about you, huh?

247
00:11:27,253 --> 00:11:30,052
When did you two
become so... buddy-buddy?

248
00:11:30,456 --> 00:11:31,788
Maybe when you hatched up a plan

249
00:11:31,925 --> 00:11:34,224
so you could keep
that baby for yourself.

250
00:11:34,827 --> 00:11:36,386
Harvey, whatever
you think of me,

251
00:11:36,729 --> 00:11:39,392
I did not plot to kill
my child's father.

252
00:11:39,732 --> 00:11:40,927
Well, someone here did!

253
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:43,298
Someone in this
room shot Jim Gordon,

254
00:11:43,436 --> 00:11:45,803
and I'm not leaving
till I find out who it was!

255
00:11:45,939 --> 00:11:49,034
Wrong! The shooter was not here!

256
00:11:49,175 --> 00:11:50,837
Look at the window, stupid!

257
00:11:50,977 --> 00:11:52,707
The shot came from outside.

258
00:11:57,984 --> 00:11:59,885
If the shooter was there...

259
00:12:00,486 --> 00:12:03,046
and the trajectory was here...

260
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:04,782
Jim was...

261
00:12:05,358 --> 00:12:06,382
then the bullet...

262
00:12:11,030 --> 00:12:12,030
Uh-huh.

263
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:17,461
I'm gonna find out who this was,

264
00:12:18,137 --> 00:12:20,470
and when I do, there's
gonna be hell to pay.

265
00:12:22,008 --> 00:12:23,237
Harvey.

266
00:12:25,311 --> 00:12:26,973
Is there anything I can do?

267
00:12:27,247 --> 00:12:30,740
Yeah. You can keep the
gangs from tearing the city apart.

268
00:12:32,452 --> 00:12:33,750
(door closes)

269
00:12:35,788 --> 00:12:36,983
What do you want?

270
00:12:37,123 --> 00:12:38,284
You...

271
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,154
I will deal with later.

272
00:12:41,227 --> 00:12:42,227
I'm here...

273
00:12:43,196 --> 00:12:44,289
for you.

274
00:12:44,897 --> 00:12:46,092
I need you to come with me.

275
00:12:46,366 --> 00:12:47,857
Why would I do that?

276
00:12:48,201 --> 00:12:49,999
Because you love me so much.

277
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:53,296
Well, not yet, but you will.

278
00:12:53,506 --> 00:12:54,906
Don't mess with him, Ivy.

279
00:12:55,041 --> 00:12:56,407
Protecting your boyfriend?

280
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:58,277
That's cute.

281
00:12:59,212 --> 00:13:01,545
But I thought that
might happen, so...

282
00:13:02,181 --> 00:13:03,547
I brought a friend.

283
00:13:04,917 --> 00:13:06,317
<i>I stumbled across
this charming man</i>

284
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:07,452
<i>on the way over here,</i>

285
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:10,882
and apparently, you
two know each other.

286
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:12,789
Leave her out of this!

287
00:13:17,864 --> 00:13:20,834
You know, I heard you talking
about the future of Gotham...

288
00:13:21,567 --> 00:13:23,559
but Gotham will
be what <i>I</i> decide.

289
00:13:25,071 --> 00:13:26,539
A green world.

290
00:13:28,508 --> 00:13:30,477
Won't that be beautiful?

291
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:33,939
(whispers): Gorgeous.

292
00:13:34,314 --> 00:13:35,338
(chuckles)

293
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:39,980
Bruce and I have to go.

294
00:13:41,988 --> 00:13:44,856
You always did think
you were better than me.

295
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:47,817
But without my plants,

296
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,327
you never would
have left your bed.

297
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:52,999
I made you strong again.

298
00:13:53,399 --> 00:13:54,594
Think about that

299
00:13:55,034 --> 00:13:57,936
while my friend is
cutting out your heart.

300
00:13:59,072 --> 00:14:00,973
♪♪

301
00:14:02,475 --> 00:14:04,467
(seabirds squawking)

302
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:10,550
There are so many things
I wish I could say to you.

303
00:14:11,451 --> 00:14:13,477
(monitor beeping steadily)

304
00:14:16,155 --> 00:14:18,386
So many things I
wish we could do.

305
00:14:21,894 --> 00:14:23,385
This can't be the end.

306
00:14:23,963 --> 00:14:25,090
Come on, Jim.

307
00:14:26,132 --> 00:14:27,156
Talk to me.

308
00:14:29,102 --> 00:14:30,570
Say something.

309
00:14:33,072 --> 00:14:34,072
Speak.

310
00:14:34,173 --> 00:14:36,574
- (gavel striking slowly,
rhythmically)
- No.

311
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:38,690
This isn't right. I
shouldn't be here.

312
00:14:38,911 --> 00:14:40,923
- JUDGE: <i>Silence! Silence!</i>
- You have to listen to me.

313
00:14:40,947 --> 00:14:44,179
The prosecution will now
give its opening remarks.

314
00:14:46,986 --> 00:14:50,445
Your Honor, Jim Gordon's
crimes are a matter of public record.

315
00:14:51,991 --> 00:14:54,051
<i>He's failed Gotham
at every turn.</i>

316
00:14:54,627 --> 00:14:57,028
He failed to
clean up the city...

317
00:14:58,131 --> 00:15:01,033
failed to stop the bridges
from being destroyed,

318
00:15:01,434 --> 00:15:05,030
failed to protect those
poor, innocent souls

319
00:15:05,171 --> 00:15:08,005
in the refuge he
himself created...

320
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:09,908
Haven.

321
00:15:09,942 --> 00:15:10,966
I tried.

322
00:15:11,277 --> 00:15:12,540
- I did the best...
<i>- Silence!</i>

323
00:15:12,678 --> 00:15:14,078
(gavel bangs)

324
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:18,150
One more outburst and
you will be held in contempt.

325
00:15:22,688 --> 00:15:23,917
I'm hurt.

326
00:15:25,358 --> 00:15:26,451
I need help. Please.

327
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,555
Continue.

328
00:15:29,529 --> 00:15:34,024
The issue here is not
how many people have died

329
00:15:34,167 --> 00:15:35,635
because of Jim Gordon,

330
00:15:36,002 --> 00:15:37,937
<i>but how many more must die</i>

331
00:15:38,070 --> 00:15:40,335
<i>in order to satisfy
his need to be a hero.</i>

332
00:15:41,140 --> 00:15:42,301
Therefore we pose

333
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:44,411
one simple question:

334
00:15:46,212 --> 00:15:48,579
Are the people in
Jim Gordon's life

335
00:15:49,282 --> 00:15:51,979
better off with him alive

336
00:15:52,552 --> 00:15:53,952
<i>or dead?</i>

337
00:15:55,254 --> 00:15:56,654
I think I'm dying.

338
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:59,034
PROSECUTOR: <i>The
prosecution would like to call</i>

339
00:15:59,058 --> 00:16:00,651
<i>its first witness, Your Honor.</i>

340
00:16:04,263 --> 00:16:06,061
Dr. Lee Thompkins.

341
00:16:06,199 --> 00:16:08,191
♪♪

342
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:14,467
(rapid beeping)

343
00:16:16,309 --> 00:16:17,504
Come on, Jim.

344
00:16:17,743 --> 00:16:19,006
Hold on.

345
00:16:19,078 --> 00:16:20,478
(door opens)

346
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:22,073
How is he?

347
00:16:22,215 --> 00:16:23,308
Touch and go.

348
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:26,219
(sighs): He's stable for now.

349
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:28,330
I removed all the
bullet fragments,

350
00:16:28,354 --> 00:16:30,346
but something keeps
pulling him down.

351
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:31,583
Where are the fragments?

352
00:16:32,425 --> 00:16:34,223
(monitor beeping steadily)

353
00:16:42,368 --> 00:16:43,427
What is it?

354
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:45,297
"V.Z."

355
00:16:46,639 --> 00:16:47,663
Victor Zsasz.

356
00:16:50,309 --> 00:16:51,709
(horn honks in distance)

357
00:16:52,044 --> 00:16:53,410
Okey-dokey.

358
00:16:54,647 --> 00:16:55,512
Time to boogie.

359
00:16:55,648 --> 00:16:57,617
♪♪

360
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:07,556
ZSASZ: Hey!

361
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:09,355
I'm only here for Gordon.

362
00:17:10,263 --> 00:17:12,027
So all of you stay down.

363
00:17:12,431 --> 00:17:14,024
<i>'Cause I see anyone...</i>

364
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,128
and, you know...

365
00:17:17,770 --> 00:17:18,770
bang.

366
00:17:18,804 --> 00:17:20,033
Oi, oi!

367
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:25,504
Now, I heard you were
looking for Jim Gordon.

368
00:17:25,745 --> 00:17:26,745
(weakly): <i>Uh-huh.</i>

369
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:33,449
Listen, I know we have history.

370
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:36,486
Let's just let
bygones be bygones.

371
00:17:36,622 --> 00:17:37,646
Yeah, right.

372
00:17:38,324 --> 00:17:40,350
You did this to my face.

373
00:17:40,493 --> 00:17:41,493
<i>Whatever.</i>

374
00:17:41,594 --> 00:17:44,120
It's not like you were much
of a looker before, anyway.

375
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:47,357
(growls) Ivy says
you hurt her feelings.

376
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,798
Why would you do that!?

377
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:50,764
She's so sweet!

378
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,800
(roaring)

379
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:55,740
Ivy didn't make me strong.

380
00:17:56,142 --> 00:17:57,142
I made me strong.

381
00:17:57,276 --> 00:17:58,335
(grunts, chokes)

382
00:17:58,477 --> 00:18:00,241
Tell me where she took Bruce.

383
00:18:04,784 --> 00:18:07,219
<i>The only reason I'm
not ending you right now</i>

384
00:18:08,154 --> 00:18:09,665
is the thought of
the look on your face

385
00:18:09,689 --> 00:18:11,453
when Jim Gordon
walks through that door.

386
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,719
Because he's alive,
you son of a bitch!

387
00:18:13,859 --> 00:18:16,522
Ugh. What did you eat?

388
00:18:16,729 --> 00:18:18,254
You smell like a butcher.

389
00:18:18,598 --> 00:18:20,226
You know, I'm vegan now.

390
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:21,859
Why kill Jim now?

391
00:18:22,802 --> 00:18:23,565
Makes no sense.

392
00:18:23,703 --> 00:18:25,467
He saved your miserable ass.

393
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:29,201
He prevented Penguin
from executing you.

394
00:18:29,508 --> 00:18:32,273
If anyone, you should
be going after Cobblepot.

395
00:18:32,712 --> 00:18:34,203
Yeah, that's a good point.

396
00:18:34,547 --> 00:18:36,209
Maybe I'll do him next.

397
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:38,649
It's kind of not up to me.

398
00:18:39,285 --> 00:18:40,583
You're working for someone?

399
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:41,847
(whispers): Oh.

400
00:18:44,156 --> 00:18:45,156
Sorry.

401
00:18:45,891 --> 00:18:48,190
(grunting)

402
00:18:48,327 --> 00:18:49,351
I want a name!

403
00:18:49,528 --> 00:18:51,622
Ah, what's in a name?

404
00:18:52,431 --> 00:18:54,559
A rose by any other name
would smell as sweet.

405
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,462
You know, I'm
really taking the time

406
00:18:56,602 --> 00:18:58,468
to stop and smell
the roses these days.

407
00:18:58,604 --> 00:19:00,334
Like, actual roses.

408
00:19:00,906 --> 00:19:02,272
They're great.

409
00:19:02,408 --> 00:19:03,637
Are you high?

410
00:19:03,776 --> 00:19:04,776
On love.

411
00:19:05,211 --> 00:19:06,338
But like I said...

412
00:19:07,647 --> 00:19:08,647
my lips are sealed.

413
00:19:11,384 --> 00:19:12,909
(snaps fingers) Ivy Pepper.

414
00:19:14,420 --> 00:19:15,479
You said it, not me.

415
00:19:15,621 --> 00:19:17,613
Uh, I'm technically
not allowed to say it.

416
00:19:17,757 --> 00:19:19,385
Her name. Which
is such a bummer,

417
00:19:19,525 --> 00:19:21,619
because it's the most
beautiful name in the world.

418
00:19:21,927 --> 00:19:22,927
You watch him.

419
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:24,255
I could say it all day.

420
00:19:24,397 --> 00:19:25,797
Hey, I <i>will</i> say it all day.

421
00:19:25,931 --> 00:19:26,931
Ivy.

422
00:19:27,366 --> 00:19:28,425
Ivy Pepper.

423
00:19:28,901 --> 00:19:30,199
Mrs...

424
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,395
Ivy Pepper Zsasz.

425
00:19:31,537 --> 00:19:32,537
Oh, that sounds good.

426
00:19:40,312 --> 00:19:40,938
Here you are, Miss Thompkins.

427
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:42,942
Careful, it's...
a little bit hot.

428
00:19:44,884 --> 00:19:46,512
Forgive me, but I...

429
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:49,378
heard on the grapevine
that you and Captain Gordon

430
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:51,354
had a rather heated
exchange this morning.

431
00:19:51,490 --> 00:19:52,617
<i>Oh, God.</i>

432
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:54,352
Was it that bad?

433
00:19:54,794 --> 00:19:55,591
Apparently, it
was like a session

434
00:19:55,728 --> 00:19:56,855
of the Italian parliament.

435
00:19:57,196 --> 00:19:58,391
(sighs heavily)

436
00:20:04,570 --> 00:20:05,799
You have misgivings

437
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:08,531
about the arrival of
this child, don't you?

438
00:20:10,643 --> 00:20:12,839
What am I getting
myself into, Alfred?

439
00:20:13,579 --> 00:20:15,878
How am I supposed
to raise a child

440
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:18,514
alongside a psychopath
like Barbara Kean?

441
00:20:18,651 --> 00:20:20,813
I mean, how the hell
is this gonna work?

442
00:20:21,420 --> 00:20:23,889
But... but that's not all of it.

443
00:20:24,457 --> 00:20:27,291
If Jim and I are gonna do this,
then we have to do it together.

444
00:20:27,426 --> 00:20:28,587
You know how he is.

445
00:20:28,961 --> 00:20:29,758
I don't know what's going on

446
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:31,557
inside that man's
head sometimes.

447
00:20:31,831 --> 00:20:33,527
I think you'll find
that he needs you

448
00:20:33,666 --> 00:20:35,225
a lot more than he's letting on.

449
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:38,260
Well, I need to
hear it from him.

450
00:20:40,306 --> 00:20:43,435
I never thought that this was
how my life was going to be.

451
00:20:45,311 --> 00:20:47,337
I have no interest in
being a father myself.

452
00:20:47,947 --> 00:20:50,917
I always presumed
that I was unfit to be one.

453
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:54,519
And then I found myself...

454
00:20:55,554 --> 00:20:57,682
one night staring down
an alley at this little boy

455
00:20:57,823 --> 00:21:00,793
quite literally
shaking with fear.

456
00:21:01,794 --> 00:21:04,034
I don't know, it's funny,
isn't it, what life throws you?

457
00:21:04,597 --> 00:21:08,932
I'm keenly aware that I am not
Master Bruce's flesh and blood.

458
00:21:09,502 --> 00:21:10,834
But it's the moments.

459
00:21:12,638 --> 00:21:14,436
The little things, like...

460
00:21:14,874 --> 00:21:17,036
like when he uses a skill
that I once taught him,

461
00:21:17,376 --> 00:21:20,312
or we laugh at a joke
that only he and I share.

462
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:24,279
Those have been some of the
most ecstatic moments of my life.

463
00:21:24,650 --> 00:21:27,643
Nothing can possibly
prepare you for that joy.

464
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,615
The hows and the whats...

465
00:21:31,457 --> 00:21:33,016
you'll figure that stuff out.

466
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:35,951
What matters is this:

467
00:21:36,428 --> 00:21:38,795
you'll be an exquisite mother,

468
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:43,061
and that child, he or
she will be extraordinary...

469
00:21:44,870 --> 00:21:46,065
because of you.

470
00:21:46,672 --> 00:21:49,301
♪♪

471
00:21:50,843 --> 00:21:52,004
(sniffles)

472
00:21:52,344 --> 00:21:53,744
Thank you, Alfred.

473
00:21:58,517 --> 00:21:59,644
(sniffles)

474
00:22:04,924 --> 00:22:06,859
Jim, can you hear me?

475
00:22:09,895 --> 00:22:11,488
I'm right here,
right next to you.

476
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,696
<i>Can you feel me?</i>

477
00:22:18,537 --> 00:22:19,698
Lee?

478
00:22:19,905 --> 00:22:22,602
Dr. Lee Thompkins.

479
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:25,603
<i>You've suffered at this man's
hands more than anyone.</i>

480
00:22:26,712 --> 00:22:27,907
Broken heart,

481
00:22:29,114 --> 00:22:30,514
broken engagement.

482
00:22:31,984 --> 00:22:33,350
A lost child.

483
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:36,684
And yet, you're still with him.

484
00:22:37,890 --> 00:22:38,983
I love him.

485
00:22:39,391 --> 00:22:41,656
<i>After all the pain
he's caused you,</i>

486
00:22:42,895 --> 00:22:44,022
would your life be better,

487
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:46,764
could it not still <i>be</i> better,

488
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:48,895
without Jim Gordon?

489
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:52,702
Answer the question.

490
00:22:52,905 --> 00:22:54,785
- Lee?
- PROSECUTOR: <i>I'll ask it</i>
<i>a different way.</i>

491
00:22:54,974 --> 00:22:57,466
Would you, Dr. Lee Thompkins,

492
00:22:57,710 --> 00:23:00,805
be better off if Jim
Gordon were dead?

493
00:23:02,781 --> 00:23:03,781
I'm sorry.

494
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:07,576
Everything he touches dies.

495
00:23:08,988 --> 00:23:10,479
Prosecution rests, Your Honor.

496
00:23:13,092 --> 00:23:14,390
You made her say that.

497
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:16,595
PROSECUTOR: <i>I didn't
make her say anything.</i>

498
00:23:16,762 --> 00:23:17,923
Ask them.

499
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:20,122
(whooshing, flames hissing)

500
00:23:20,466 --> 00:23:21,525
GORDON: <i>Who are they?</i>

501
00:23:21,667 --> 00:23:24,000
PROSECUTOR: <i>More people
who trusted you, who believed you</i>

502
00:23:24,136 --> 00:23:27,538
when you said you
would protect them.

503
00:23:28,941 --> 00:23:29,965
They're from Haven.

504
00:23:32,011 --> 00:23:33,479
I think I'm dying.

505
00:23:35,047 --> 00:23:36,982
And isn't it about time?

506
00:23:40,019 --> 00:23:41,043
The verdict's in.

507
00:23:42,554 --> 00:23:43,554
You're guilty.

508
00:23:47,793 --> 00:23:49,694
(wind whistling)

509
00:23:52,164 --> 00:23:53,792
Hey, Jeff, listen to me.

510
00:23:54,033 --> 00:23:55,076
One day, you're
gonna meet someone

511
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:56,540
who's gonna totally
change your life,

512
00:23:56,802 --> 00:23:58,430
and that's gonna make you happy,

513
00:23:58,604 --> 00:24:00,505
and you deserve it.

514
00:24:03,475 --> 00:24:04,670
Or not.

515
00:24:05,978 --> 00:24:07,002
Is she here?

516
00:24:07,146 --> 00:24:08,580
She's here, isn't she?

517
00:24:11,016 --> 00:24:12,211
Sweetie.

518
00:24:13,986 --> 00:24:15,784
All I asked of you

519
00:24:16,722 --> 00:24:18,520
was to kill Jim Gordon.

520
00:24:19,158 --> 00:24:20,456
You're not angry, are you?

521
00:24:20,592 --> 00:24:22,152
'Cause I'll do it.
I'll do it right now.

522
00:24:25,030 --> 00:24:26,123
I'll do it.

523
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:28,725
You keep the cops busy.

524
00:24:30,069 --> 00:24:33,471
Luckily, the other part of my
plan is coming together nicely.

525
00:24:47,086 --> 00:24:49,021
(steam hissing)

526
00:24:58,931 --> 00:24:59,990
Lucius!

527
00:25:00,666 --> 00:25:01,666
Bruce.

528
00:25:02,001 --> 00:25:03,902
I had no idea you
were stopping by.

529
00:25:06,038 --> 00:25:07,398
I wanted to check
on your progress.

530
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:10,935
Well, the toxicity levels in
this river continue to drop.

531
00:25:11,076 --> 00:25:13,511
At this point, we'll be under
the threshold mandated

532
00:25:13,679 --> 00:25:15,511
by the government
sooner than expected.

533
00:25:15,647 --> 00:25:17,513
It's not glamorous
work, but we are helping

534
00:25:17,649 --> 00:25:19,641
to save the lives of
thousands of people.

535
00:25:19,785 --> 00:25:21,777
People. Ugh.

536
00:25:22,888 --> 00:25:25,153
I'm sorry. Did you
just say "People. Ugh"?

537
00:25:25,290 --> 00:25:27,555
Lucius, what if I
were to tell you

538
00:25:27,693 --> 00:25:30,026
I have in my possession
the most intoxicating perfume

539
00:25:30,162 --> 00:25:31,289
you'll ever smell?

540
00:25:31,697 --> 00:25:33,657
I would tell you that's
an abrupt change of topic.

541
00:25:33,766 --> 00:25:36,065
Can we go back to the part
where you said "People. Ugh"?

542
00:25:37,102 --> 00:25:38,229
(grunts)

543
00:25:38,904 --> 00:25:39,928
Mmm.

544
00:25:42,741 --> 00:25:44,903
(echoing): Oh, my... goodness.

545
00:25:44,977 --> 00:25:46,138
<i>Lucius,</i>

546
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:48,305
Ivy sent me here to get
you to shut down the plant.

547
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,148
<i>Can you do that for her?</i>

548
00:25:50,616 --> 00:25:53,176
(distorted): For Ivy? Anything.

549
00:25:53,652 --> 00:25:55,280
She is so great.

550
00:26:00,893 --> 00:26:03,692
♪ They say, they say
she's got to grow up ♪

551
00:26:03,829 --> 00:26:07,061
♪ And they say, they
say she's got to get a job ♪

552
00:26:07,199 --> 00:26:10,897
♪ I know, I know I'll
never be like the rest ♪

553
00:26:11,036 --> 00:26:13,665
♪ Of the bunch. Oh! ♪

554
00:26:14,073 --> 00:26:15,632
Raise your glasses.

555
00:26:16,909 --> 00:26:18,207
I called you all here today

556
00:26:18,343 --> 00:26:21,108
because Jim Gordon
is at death's door.

557
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:23,647
ALL: Yeah!

558
00:26:23,782 --> 00:26:25,648
For years, he has hounded us,

559
00:26:25,784 --> 00:26:27,980
beaten us, shot us.

560
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:29,247
<i>And today, he got his due.</i>

561
00:26:29,855 --> 00:26:32,290
To Jim Gordon.
May he rot in hell!

562
00:26:32,624 --> 00:26:34,650
ALL: Yeah!

563
00:26:34,793 --> 00:26:37,319
♪♪

564
00:26:38,097 --> 00:26:39,690
What exactly are you doing?

565
00:26:39,898 --> 00:26:42,197
I'm trying to keep this
city from ripping itself apart.

566
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:46,269
So this has nothing to do
with your feelings for Jim?

567
00:26:46,738 --> 00:26:49,037
What if Ed fails, and
we are stuck here?

568
00:26:49,808 --> 00:26:51,868
<i>This will put us in
Gordon's good graces.</i>

569
00:26:52,111 --> 00:26:53,909
Consider it a backup plan.

570
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:56,275
♪♪

571
00:26:57,015 --> 00:26:58,074
<i>Listen up!</i>

572
00:26:58,750 --> 00:27:01,151
Now to the real reason
I brought you all here.

573
00:27:02,788 --> 00:27:03,312
<i>I want you</i>

574
00:27:03,655 --> 00:27:06,352
to agree to an immediate truce.

575
00:27:06,692 --> 00:27:08,354
(laughing): Get out of here.

576
00:27:08,694 --> 00:27:12,153
And what if, instead, we
shoot you and take your club?

577
00:27:13,332 --> 00:27:14,857
I don't think so.

578
00:27:15,267 --> 00:27:17,065
See, those drinks
I just gave you...

579
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:18,803
They're poisoned.

580
00:27:19,171 --> 00:27:22,403
<i>And you had two shots
before everyone got here.</i>

581
00:27:22,941 --> 00:27:25,001
So that should be
taking effect around...

582
00:27:25,277 --> 00:27:27,769
(muffled groaning)

583
00:27:29,748 --> 00:27:31,148
(choking)

584
00:27:31,917 --> 00:27:33,408
- (indistinct muttering)
- now.

585
00:27:33,785 --> 00:27:36,254
The rest of you have 48
hours before you'll need

586
00:27:36,388 --> 00:27:38,380
<i>the antidote, which
I will deliver to you,</i>

587
00:27:38,757 --> 00:27:40,726
<i>provided you go
back to your territories,</i>

588
00:27:40,859 --> 00:27:43,920
play nice, and send
me all your guns. Deal?

589
00:27:45,998 --> 00:27:47,364
I said, "Deal?"

590
00:27:47,699 --> 00:27:49,258
(all voicing assent)

591
00:27:49,401 --> 00:27:50,926
- Now get out of here!
- MAN:
<i>All right.</i>

592
00:27:51,069 --> 00:27:53,095
- Yeah. Out.
- Come on.

593
00:27:54,973 --> 00:27:55,973
Hmm.

594
00:27:56,675 --> 00:27:58,439
Jim will be so pleased.

595
00:27:59,244 --> 00:28:01,338
Keep your friends close,
and your enemies closer.

596
00:28:02,114 --> 00:28:04,242
Isn't that right... Pengy?

597
00:28:18,063 --> 00:28:19,759
Once I reverse the system,

598
00:28:19,898 --> 00:28:22,333
all the toxin we pulled from
the river will be rereleased,

599
00:28:22,467 --> 00:28:24,436
and the overload
should destroy the filters.

600
00:28:24,970 --> 00:28:26,336
In a matter of minutes,

601
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:29,334
the entire facility
will be inoperable.

602
00:28:30,742 --> 00:28:31,300
There.

603
00:28:31,443 --> 00:28:33,844
- (alarms sounding)
- Perfect.

604
00:28:33,979 --> 00:28:36,039
Ivy's gonna be so happy.

605
00:28:36,348 --> 00:28:37,441
You think so?

606
00:28:38,083 --> 00:28:40,382
MAN (over P.A.):
<i>Security breach. Zone 1.</i>

607
00:28:41,186 --> 00:28:42,313
That's odd.

608
00:28:53,198 --> 00:28:54,325
Selina.

609
00:28:56,735 --> 00:28:57,794
I'll take care of it.

610
00:28:58,203 --> 00:28:59,227
Okay.

611
00:29:01,039 --> 00:29:02,507
All right, listen up!

612
00:29:03,075 --> 00:29:06,739
I know you're probably
familiar with Ivy Pepper.

613
00:29:06,945 --> 00:29:08,056
In fact, you were probably here

614
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:11,175
when she hypnotized the
whole frigging precinct, okay?

615
00:29:11,316 --> 00:29:12,807
She is on the loose,

616
00:29:12,985 --> 00:29:15,284
and we've got to find
her and take her down.

617
00:29:15,454 --> 00:29:16,820
Actually, fellas,

618
00:29:17,022 --> 00:29:19,253
- she's already here!
- (gun chamber clicking)

619
00:29:19,391 --> 00:29:21,417
(indistinct shouting)

620
00:29:24,963 --> 00:29:27,398
That's right. Ivy
came and freed me.

621
00:29:27,532 --> 00:29:29,865
That is true love for you.

622
00:29:31,436 --> 00:29:34,406
She really understands
what makes me tick.

623
00:29:34,773 --> 00:29:36,013
- Don't worry, though.
- (yells)

624
00:29:36,141 --> 00:29:37,336
I'm just a distraction

625
00:29:37,476 --> 00:29:40,241
so she can finish off
Jim once and for all.

626
00:29:40,412 --> 00:29:42,313
You know, that's how
great couples work.

627
00:29:44,249 --> 00:29:45,689
Maybe I shouldn't
have told you that.

628
00:29:46,118 --> 00:29:47,177
Oh, well.

629
00:29:54,526 --> 00:29:56,461
(distant, rapid gunfire)

630
00:29:57,329 --> 00:29:59,195
- I'm sorry,
Miss Thompkins.
- I know. Go.

631
00:29:59,331 --> 00:30:00,492
Thank you, Alfred.

632
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:02,993
Come on, Jim.

633
00:30:03,435 --> 00:30:04,459
Can you hear me?

634
00:30:04,936 --> 00:30:06,029
Stay with me.

635
00:30:06,571 --> 00:30:07,971
(echoing): Stay with me, Jim.

636
00:30:08,106 --> 00:30:09,938
(indistinct chatter)

637
00:30:12,978 --> 00:30:13,570
BULLOCK: Jim!

638
00:30:13,912 --> 00:30:15,972
(laughs) Want a drink?

639
00:30:16,114 --> 00:30:18,310
Alvarez makes a
hell of a Mai Tai.

640
00:30:19,084 --> 00:30:20,450
I can barely feel my face.

641
00:30:21,019 --> 00:30:22,351
Harvey, what is this?

642
00:30:22,921 --> 00:30:24,253
It's your wake.

643
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:26,155
Pretty nice turn-out, huh?

644
00:30:26,892 --> 00:30:30,420
♪ For he's a jolly good fellow ♪

645
00:30:30,562 --> 00:30:32,202
- ♪ For he's a jolly good ♪
- GORDON:
Stop.

646
00:30:32,297 --> 00:30:33,297
♪ Fellow ♪

647
00:30:33,365 --> 00:30:36,335
♪ For he's a jolly good fellow ♪

648
00:30:36,468 --> 00:30:37,561
(snorting)

649
00:30:37,903 --> 00:30:39,394
(scattered laughter)

650
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:41,905
♪ Which nobody can deny. ♪

651
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:43,235
(laughter)

652
00:30:43,375 --> 00:30:44,866
Wake?

653
00:30:45,010 --> 00:30:46,154
(piano continues playing tune)

654
00:30:46,178 --> 00:30:47,407
I'm not dead yet.

655
00:30:47,946 --> 00:30:49,938
Well, be a little
bit of a bummer

656
00:30:50,115 --> 00:30:52,107
to have it after you
died, don't you think?

657
00:30:53,218 --> 00:30:54,948
I'm gonna have a kid, Harvey.

658
00:30:57,222 --> 00:31:00,124
How do I protect that child
when everything around me dies?

659
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:03,160
<i>Harvey?</i>

660
00:31:05,564 --> 00:31:07,260
WILL: <i>That's a good question.</i>

661
00:31:12,037 --> 00:31:13,061
Will.

662
00:31:13,905 --> 00:31:15,874
You said I'd be safe in Haven.

663
00:31:16,375 --> 00:31:17,434
I trusted you.

664
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:19,134
<i>I know.</i>

665
00:31:19,478 --> 00:31:20,912
I did my best.

666
00:31:22,114 --> 00:31:24,276
Your best never
seems good enough.

667
00:31:25,016 --> 00:31:26,348
It's time to go.

668
00:31:34,459 --> 00:31:35,819
- (beeping)
- THOMPKINS:
<i>No, no, no.</i>

669
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:37,774
- No, no, no, no. Jim.
- (long, continuous beep)

670
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:39,874
- Where's my adrenaline?
- (distant, rapid gunfire)

671
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:41,161
Oh...

672
00:31:47,072 --> 00:31:49,473
Oh, looks like Victor
succeeded after all.

673
00:31:55,981 --> 00:31:58,007
I guess I'll have to
settle for killing you.

674
00:32:03,955 --> 00:32:04,581
I can tell you one thing.

675
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:07,984
I am sick and tired of getting
shot at in my own precinct.

676
00:32:09,194 --> 00:32:10,685
Hey, what the
bloody hell's going on?

677
00:32:11,029 --> 00:32:12,440
I thought you had
this lunatic locked up.

678
00:32:12,464 --> 00:32:14,330
Ivy broke him out and
gave him an arsenal.

679
00:32:14,633 --> 00:32:17,193
But I have an idea. I got to get
to the storeroom. Give me cover.

680
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:18,936
Alvarez, go!

681
00:32:19,237 --> 00:32:20,705
(grunts)

682
00:32:24,409 --> 00:32:25,934
(grunting)

683
00:32:26,077 --> 00:32:27,101
(gasps)

684
00:32:27,279 --> 00:32:28,645
(panting)

685
00:32:29,014 --> 00:32:30,014
Why are you doing this?

686
00:32:30,315 --> 00:32:31,943
What has Jim ever done to you?

687
00:32:32,417 --> 00:32:35,649
Gotham has a chance
to be born anew.

688
00:32:36,421 --> 00:32:38,049
To return to what it was

689
00:32:38,190 --> 00:32:41,649
before people ripped down the
trees and paved over the earth.

690
00:32:42,093 --> 00:32:43,638
He's trying to reunify
with the mainland

691
00:32:43,662 --> 00:32:44,721
to save all these people.

692
00:32:45,063 --> 00:32:46,224
A return to filth.

693
00:32:47,332 --> 00:32:48,332
Pollution.

694
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:51,125
He's fighting for
death, while I...

695
00:32:51,703 --> 00:32:52,966
promise life...

696
00:32:53,472 --> 00:32:54,997
in its purest form.

697
00:32:59,277 --> 00:33:00,142
Is that your plan?

698
00:33:00,278 --> 00:33:02,372
To have the plants take
over Gotham by killing Jim?

699
00:33:03,148 --> 00:33:04,980
Oh, killing Gordon's
just the first part.

700
00:33:05,116 --> 00:33:07,517
Bruce Wayne is
taking care of the rest.

701
00:33:08,019 --> 00:33:10,579
- For what it's worth,
I am sorry.
- For what?

702
00:33:16,294 --> 00:33:17,387
(gasping breath)

703
00:33:18,730 --> 00:33:20,358
This pain is nothing

704
00:33:21,032 --> 00:33:23,297
compared to what
you are about to feel.

705
00:33:25,470 --> 00:33:27,496
Say good-bye... to
Jim Gordon for me.

706
00:33:27,639 --> 00:33:28,368
No!

707
00:33:28,507 --> 00:33:29,668
<i>No, no, no, no, no!</i>

708
00:33:30,308 --> 00:33:31,308
No!

709
00:33:33,411 --> 00:33:34,435
Jim.

710
00:33:39,684 --> 00:33:40,549
Selina, you're wasting

711
00:33:40,685 --> 00:33:41,448
your time.

712
00:33:41,586 --> 00:33:43,418
Bruce, you have to
snap out of Ivy's spell.

713
00:33:43,555 --> 00:33:45,285
- This is not you.
- You're wrong.

714
00:33:45,423 --> 00:33:46,652
Ivy's given me a purpose.

715
00:33:47,225 --> 00:33:48,249
(grunting)

716
00:33:48,393 --> 00:33:50,794
Stop! Stop! I don't
want to fight you!

717
00:33:51,530 --> 00:33:54,159
What are you gonna do?
Kill everything in Gotham?

718
00:33:54,399 --> 00:33:56,197
The toxins will only
kill all the people.

719
00:33:56,601 --> 00:33:58,126
The plants will
adapt; they always do.

720
00:33:58,403 --> 00:34:00,395
- Can you hear what
that sounds like?
- Yeah.

721
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,039
It sounds great!

722
00:34:05,577 --> 00:34:07,205
(coughing)

723
00:34:08,146 --> 00:34:10,479
(panting)

724
00:34:11,316 --> 00:34:13,342
I guess I shouldn't
be surprised.

725
00:34:13,685 --> 00:34:16,086
You don't care about Gotham.
You're gonna leave anyway.

726
00:34:19,190 --> 00:34:20,453
What about the rest of us, huh?

727
00:34:20,792 --> 00:34:22,055
The ones who are gonna be

728
00:34:22,193 --> 00:34:23,491
stuck here without you?!

729
00:34:23,795 --> 00:34:24,795
Selina...

730
00:34:25,463 --> 00:34:28,456
(both gasping for breath)

731
00:34:28,600 --> 00:34:30,398
<i>Selina... I'm okay.</i>

732
00:34:30,535 --> 00:34:32,504
- Bruce, I'm so sorry.
- We got to stop
Lucius.

733
00:34:32,637 --> 00:34:34,196
- Come on.
- Okay.

734
00:34:34,806 --> 00:34:35,603
(grunts)

735
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:37,231
(alarm blaring)

736
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:39,640
Lucius! You have
to stop the shutdown.

737
00:34:42,113 --> 00:34:43,706
Oh, no, I can't do that.

738
00:34:43,848 --> 00:34:45,578
Ivy will be so mad.

739
00:34:45,717 --> 00:34:48,744
Listen to me, I-I used Ivy's
perfume to hypnotize you.

740
00:34:49,154 --> 00:34:50,154
She's using you.

741
00:34:50,522 --> 00:34:51,683
No.

742
00:34:52,724 --> 00:34:54,454
Ivy would never do that.

743
00:34:54,793 --> 00:34:58,321
We're perfectly bonded,
like... carbon and oxygen

744
00:34:58,463 --> 00:34:59,463
or hydrogen

745
00:34:59,531 --> 00:35:02,228
<i>- and oxygen...</i>
- We do not have time
for this.

746
00:35:02,367 --> 00:35:03,367
I'm sorry.

747
00:35:04,736 --> 00:35:05,736
(grunts)

748
00:35:07,806 --> 00:35:09,536
- (flips switch)
- There.

749
00:35:09,708 --> 00:35:11,199
Oh, you kicked me in the head.

750
00:35:11,343 --> 00:35:12,811
I didn't have a choice, Lucius.

751
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:14,610
Bruce, where's Ivy?

752
00:35:18,683 --> 00:35:20,345
She was headed to the GCPD.

753
00:35:24,222 --> 00:35:25,850
I wonder what Ivy's
doing right now.

754
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:28,559
BULLOCK: <i>Hey, lover boy.</i>

755
00:35:32,764 --> 00:35:34,289
Are you serious right now?

756
00:35:34,432 --> 00:35:35,730
As a heart attack.

757
00:35:42,173 --> 00:35:43,664
(chuckles)

758
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:44,808
What an idiot.

759
00:35:46,511 --> 00:35:47,877
- (Bullock yelling)
- Oh, my...

760
00:35:51,750 --> 00:35:52,911
(grunts)

761
00:35:56,554 --> 00:35:57,715
Ah, that felt good.

762
00:35:58,189 --> 00:35:59,248
Come on, Jim.

763
00:35:59,391 --> 00:36:01,231
You fight for everyone
else. You never give up.

764
00:36:01,326 --> 00:36:02,885
Fight for yourself,
Jim. Come on!

765
00:36:09,534 --> 00:36:11,469
(thunder crashing)

766
00:36:17,308 --> 00:36:18,833
(door creaking)

767
00:36:20,645 --> 00:36:21,874
(thunder crashing)

768
00:36:25,617 --> 00:36:26,846
It's time.

769
00:36:40,498 --> 00:36:41,932
(thunder crashing)

770
00:36:42,634 --> 00:36:43,634
THOMPKINS (echoing): <i>Jim.</i>

771
00:36:52,310 --> 00:36:53,310
<i>Lee.</i>

772
00:36:54,446 --> 00:36:55,446
<i>Is that...?</i>

773
00:36:55,847 --> 00:36:56,906
Yes.

774
00:36:59,350 --> 00:37:00,841
Do you want to...?

775
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:07,283
I don't know.

776
00:37:09,394 --> 00:37:10,794
I don't know that I can.

777
00:37:12,997 --> 00:37:14,226
Oh, I see.

778
00:37:15,366 --> 00:37:16,857
- No!
- Good-bye, Jim.

779
00:37:17,535 --> 00:37:18,400
<i>No!</i>

780
00:37:18,536 --> 00:37:19,902
I want to live!

781
00:37:20,438 --> 00:37:21,531
<i>I want to live!</i>

782
00:37:21,673 --> 00:37:22,868
It's too late.

783
00:37:24,309 --> 00:37:25,572
No! I want to live!

784
00:37:26,444 --> 00:37:27,742
(screaming)

785
00:37:27,879 --> 00:37:29,006
(monitor beeping rapidly)

786
00:37:29,347 --> 00:37:30,747
(baby bawling)

787
00:37:31,449 --> 00:37:33,247
(gasping breaths)

788
00:37:33,785 --> 00:37:35,276
(beeping slows)

789
00:37:35,520 --> 00:37:37,512
(gasping breath) Lee.

790
00:37:37,789 --> 00:37:39,690
Don't move. Don't move.

791
00:37:41,659 --> 00:37:42,888
How do you feel?

792
00:37:44,028 --> 00:37:45,826
Like I almost died.

793
00:37:47,332 --> 00:37:48,527
Well, you didn't.

794
00:37:49,334 --> 00:37:50,927
You fought. You came back to me.

795
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:52,567
Because I need you.

796
00:37:54,973 --> 00:37:55,973
<i>Lee...</i>

797
00:37:56,674 --> 00:37:58,575
- this child...
- It's okay.

798
00:37:59,744 --> 00:38:01,440
It's okay to be scared.

799
00:38:04,649 --> 00:38:06,129
The only thing
scarier than doing this

800
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,912
is doing it without you.

801
00:38:12,524 --> 00:38:14,015
Can I ask you something?

802
00:38:19,330 --> 00:38:21,799
♪♪

803
00:38:21,933 --> 00:38:23,902
(bell tolling)

804
00:38:29,574 --> 00:38:31,406
♪♪

805
00:38:31,476 --> 00:38:33,411
(indistinct chatter)

806
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:44,086
BRUCE: He seems nervous.

807
00:38:44,455 --> 00:38:45,479
SELINA: I know.

808
00:38:45,757 --> 00:38:47,089
He should be thrilled.

809
00:38:48,660 --> 00:38:51,596
Marrying a woman who's smarter
<i>and</i> better-looking than him.

810
00:38:55,033 --> 00:38:56,968
Selina, while we were fighting,

811
00:38:57,435 --> 00:38:59,313
when I was hypnotized,
you talked about me leaving...

812
00:38:59,337 --> 00:39:00,337
Quiet.

813
00:39:00,905 --> 00:39:02,100
Here she comes.

814
00:39:04,776 --> 00:39:06,711
♪♪

815
00:39:27,432 --> 00:39:29,992
You may sit. (chuckles)

816
00:39:33,538 --> 00:39:34,403
BULLOCK: <i>I'm just gonna say,</i>

817
00:39:34,539 --> 00:39:36,739
this isn't gonna be some
long, drawn-out, tearful affair

818
00:39:36,841 --> 00:39:38,018
like you all are used to, okay?

819
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:39,322
This is gonna be
a short wedding.

820
00:39:39,444 --> 00:39:41,913
I'm gonna try and make it
quick so we can all get to the bar.

821
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:44,106
- (laughter)
<i>- Okay?</i>

822
00:39:45,083 --> 00:39:46,949
<i>I first met a young Jim Gordon</i>

823
00:39:47,719 --> 00:39:49,415
when he was a, uh...

824
00:39:49,554 --> 00:39:51,489
pain-in-the-ass, moralistic

825
00:39:51,623 --> 00:39:53,683
<i>- rookie detective.</i>
- (laughter)

826
00:39:54,025 --> 00:39:57,587
In the years since, he's
evolved into a pain-in-the-ass,

827
00:39:57,729 --> 00:39:59,391
moralistic captain.

828
00:40:00,498 --> 00:40:03,161
<i>I'd say he's my best friend,</i>

829
00:40:03,501 --> 00:40:06,494
but in truth, he's
my <i>only</i> friend.

830
00:40:08,773 --> 00:40:10,537
So we'll skip that.

831
00:40:10,909 --> 00:40:13,037
Uh, on to Lee.

832
00:40:13,945 --> 00:40:15,777
<i>Lee's always had his back.</i>

833
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:18,042
Except for the time
when she was infected

834
00:40:18,182 --> 00:40:21,516
with the crazy-making
virus and she tried to kill him,

835
00:40:21,653 --> 00:40:22,746
<i>but that's love.</i>

836
00:40:23,988 --> 00:40:25,513
<i>But I will say,</i>

837
00:40:25,857 --> 00:40:27,985
if there's one beautiful
thing that's happened

838
00:40:28,126 --> 00:40:31,119
<i>over these last few crazy years,</i>

839
00:40:31,462 --> 00:40:34,762
it's that these two
people met each other.

840
00:40:35,466 --> 00:40:36,729
<i>And that truly is...</i>

841
00:40:37,568 --> 00:40:38,866
<i>a beautiful thing.</i>

842
00:40:40,905 --> 00:40:42,806
Jim, will you please
take Lee's hand?

843
00:40:43,975 --> 00:40:44,975
(clears throat)

844
00:40:45,810 --> 00:40:49,508
<i>Do you, Jim Gordon,
take Lee Thompkins to be</i>

845
00:40:49,847 --> 00:40:51,475
<i>your lawfully wedded wife,</i>

846
00:40:51,616 --> 00:40:53,050
to have and to hold,

847
00:40:53,751 --> 00:40:55,049
from this day forward,

848
00:40:55,687 --> 00:40:57,019
<i>for better, for worse,</i>

849
00:40:57,622 --> 00:40:59,557
<i>for richer, for poorer,</i>

850
00:41:00,625 --> 00:41:02,958
in sickness and in health,

851
00:41:03,761 --> 00:41:05,024
to love and cherish

852
00:41:05,630 --> 00:41:06,928
<i>till death do you part?</i>

853
00:41:07,966 --> 00:41:09,127
I do.

854
00:41:11,736 --> 00:41:13,762
And you, Lee Thompkins,
do you do the same?

855
00:41:15,039 --> 00:41:16,473
Sure, Harvey.

856
00:41:17,608 --> 00:41:18,769
I do.

857
00:41:21,579 --> 00:41:23,571
By the power vested in me...

858
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:26,713
by absolutely no one...

859
00:41:26,851 --> 00:41:27,910
(laughter)

860
00:41:28,052 --> 00:41:29,748
I now pronounce you

861
00:41:30,555 --> 00:41:32,956
husband and wife.

862
00:41:33,224 --> 00:41:37,559
(cheering, whistling)

863
00:41:37,695 --> 00:41:40,096
♪♪

864
00:41:56,047 --> 00:41:57,071
What?

865
00:41:58,950 --> 00:42:00,919
♪♪

866
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:13,965
<i>(applause fades)</i>

867
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:20,831
And now Jim Gordon
and Lee Thompkins

868
00:42:21,005 --> 00:42:23,565
are man and wife.

869
00:42:24,142 --> 00:42:27,704
<i>Thank God you held
the city together so that</i>

870
00:42:27,845 --> 00:42:30,314
this blessed event
could take place.

871
00:42:33,251 --> 00:42:34,742
<i>It was never gonna work.</i>

872
00:42:36,754 --> 00:42:37,551
What?

873
00:42:37,688 --> 00:42:40,248
<i>Controlling the gangs
was not a backup plan.</i>

874
00:42:41,059 --> 00:42:43,028
You... saw a chance

875
00:42:43,161 --> 00:42:46,063
to convince James Gordon
that you had changed.

876
00:42:47,165 --> 00:42:49,259
But he will never see you

877
00:42:49,600 --> 00:42:52,001
<i>as anything but a
dangerous woman</i>

878
00:42:52,136 --> 00:42:54,002
<i>keeping his child from him.</i>

879
00:42:54,806 --> 00:42:56,206
Then I'd best be long gone

880
00:42:56,340 --> 00:42:58,605
before he can do
anything about it.

881
00:43:01,045 --> 00:43:04,209
He will hunt you till
the ends of the earth.

882
00:43:04,882 --> 00:43:05,882
(chuckles)

883
00:43:09,287 --> 00:43:10,585
Let him.
